-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",391,{
[12481]="7002BFD9\n1\tTalk to Céola at Etheburg in the Brown Lands\tCéola is at Etheburg in the Brown Lands, south-east of Aculf's camp. Aculf asked you to warn Céola, the commander of the border-guard in the Brown Lands, of the Khundolar's impending invasion.\n",
[12482]="7002FD53\n1\tScout the croft to the east of Garsfeld\030Scout the croft to the south-west of Garsfeld\030Scout the croft to the south of Garsfeld\tThe crofts can be found to the east, south, and south-west of Garsfeld. Gísling wishes for you to scout the three largest crofts around Garsfeld to discover how much damage has been dealt to this season's crops.\n2\tTalk to Gísling\tGísling is in the Mead Hall of Garsfeld. You should return to Gísling with news of your discoveries.\n",
[12483]="7005AB13\n1\tDefeat Grimdóth the Bitter\030Place a fresh ram to lure Fólnith the Pale from the sky and defeat him\tMolkha has asked you to slay Fólnith the Pale and Grimdóth the Bitter, siblings of Vethúg Wintermind. One can be found at the top of Flogalith, the other flies over the frozen lake and will need to be lured from the sky.\n2\tTalk to Molkha in the valley\tThe two elder drakes have been slain! You should report your success to Molkha. Molkha can be found on the frozen lake south-west of Fellgát.\n",
[12484]="700681BD\n1\tDiscover Ghar Jâdam\tA fierce sekbir stands above the rest.\n2\tDefeat the sekbir brute\tA fierce sekbir stands above the rest. Defeat the sekbir brute in Ghar Jâdam.\n",
[12485]="700654AE\n1\tTalk to Langwen\tOthanar has asked you to speak with Langwen, who has been asking for assistance. Langwen can be found by a fountain in one of the gardens in the Harlond.\n2\tPick up the bag full of banners\tLangwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond. You should pick up the nearby bag full of banners. The bag is next to Langwen, in the Harlond.\n3\tReplace tattered banners (total: 5)\tLangwen has asked you to replace shredded banners atop the towers of Rammas Echor in the Harlond.\n4\tReturn to Langwen\tYou have taken down the tattered banners and replaced them with proud black flags bearing the white tree of Gondor. You should let Langwen know that her new banners fly from the towers' heights. Langwen is in the Harlond.\n",
[12486]="70071E8A\n1\tSpeak with Quartermaster Aralath in Sul Madásh\tAfter speaking with Dithúrim, she directed you to speak with Quartermaster Aralath. He will provide further information in how we can assist the Kintai in Adagím.\n2\tSpeak with Dithúrim in Sul Madásh\tQuartermaster Aralath informed you of how you can assist the Kintai and bid you return to Dithúrim for final instruction and a gift.\n",
[12487]="70071E06\n1\tRecover Chronicles of the Tarsâri, Vol. I\030Recover Chronicles of the Tarsâri, Vol. II\030Recover Chronicles of the Tarsâri, Vol. IV\030Defeat Tarsâri within the Blade-horn (total: 11)\tRecover historical texts about the Tarsâri in Bâdrasag, the Blade-horn.\n2\tSearch for the missing volume of 'Chronicles of the Tarsâri'\tSearch for the missing volume of 'Chronicles of the Tarsâri'.\n3\tDefeat the Tarsâri Veiled One\tDefeat the Tarsâri Veiled One in the Blade-horn.\n",
[12488]="7004E1DD\n1\tTalk to King Thranduil\tKing Thranduil can be found within Felegoth. Concerned that none of the visions you were granted have come to pass, King Thorin III has asked you to seek King Thranduil's counsel on what is to be done.\n2\tTravel to Caras Galadhon and seek Lady Galadriel in the Court of Celeborn\tThe Court of Celeborn can be found within Caras Galadhon. King Thranduil has asked you to seek the counsel of Lady Galadriel in Caras Galadhon. NOTE: If you have not previously entered Caras Galadhon, you may use a rope near the entrance to enter the city. If you have not begun the Court of Lothlórien allegiance, you may speak to one of the Galadhrim beneath the great mallorn in the centre of Caras Galadhon to enter the Court of Celeborn.\n3\tTalk to Lady Galadriel\tLady Galadriel can be found in the Court of Celeborn. You have come to the Court of Celeborn and should now seek Lady Galadriel's counsel.\n4\tTravel to Galadriel's Garden\tGaladriel's Garden can be found in the south-eastern reaches of Caras Galadhon. Lady Galadriel has decided to consult the Mirror of Galadriel to determine if Karazgar has indeed returned to Dol Guldur.\n5\tTalk to Lady Galadriel\tLady Galadriel is standing in her garden. You have arrived at Galadriel's Garden and should now speak to Lady Galadriel and learn what she has seen.\n",
[12489]="70037095\n1\tTalk to Lúfa when you are ready to defend her\tLúfa is at Ordlac's house in Oserley. You should speak with Lúfa when you are prepared to defend her against the servants of the White Hand.\n2\tTalk to Lúfa in Ordlac's house\tLúfa is at Ordlac's house in Oserley. You should speak with Lúfa now that you have foiled the attempt upon her life.\n",
[12490]="700430D8\n1\tTalk to Angbor outside Tumladen\tLord Angbor can be found just outside Tumladen in northern Upper Lebennin. Lady Terenis has threatened to imprison you unless you or Lord Angbor tell her the truth of the battle at Pelargir.\n",
[12491]="70037164\n1\tBring Lúfa's favour to Torferth at Torsbury\tWhen you come to Torsbury, you should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.\n2\tTorferth is in Torsbury, west of Oserley. When you come to Torsbury, you should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.\t\n3\tBring Lúfa's favour to Torferth in Tordag's camp\tTorferth is in Tordag's camp, west of Oserley. You should deliver Lúfa's favour to Torferth.\n",
[12492]="7003709E\n1\tBring the dagger to Dudsig\tDudsig is near the stables in Oserley. Lúfa bade you take the dagger you recovered to Dudsig and report that you were successful in your duty.\n",
[12493]="70037093\n1\tTalk to Dudsig and obtain the key to Ordlac's house\tDudsig is near the stables in Oserley. Ordlac has instructed you to obtain the key to his house from Dudsig.\n2\tTalk to Lúfa at Ordlac's house\tOrdlac's house is near the Oserley stable, on the road to the Mead Hall. Dudsig gave you the key to Thane Ordlac's house and bade you fulfill your duty there.\n",
[12494]="70037092\n1\tCollect wine from the table\tThe wine is on the table in Thane Ordlac's house. Lúfa has asked you to bring her a cup of wine to ease her thirst while she tells you her tale.\n2\tBring the cup of wine to Lúfa\tLúfa is at Thane Ordlac's house in Oserley. Lúfa awaits the wine she requested from you.\n3\tTalk to Lúfa in Ordlac's house\tLúfa is at Thane Ordlac's house in Oserley. Lúfa has finished her tale and wishes to speak with you again.\n",
[12495]="7006441F\n1\tComplete 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty\tComplete 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin' on any difficulty. Use the Instance Finder to enter 'Sagroth, Lair of Vermin'.\n2\tTalk to Lágsaith in Bail Avarc\tLágsaith has concluded her tale. You should talk to her in Bail Avarc.\n",
[12496]="70040EE7\n1\tLook to Dol Amroth in the west from Amon Lontir\tDol Amroth can be viewed to the west of Amon Lontir. Boradan has asked you to look from the beacon to Dol Amroth.\n2\tTalk to Boradan\tBoradan can be found on the beacon, Amon Lontir, just outside Ost Lontir. You have looked upon Dol Amroth and should now speak to Boradan.\n3\tLook to Edhellond in the north from Amon Lontir\tEdhellond can be viewed to the north of Amon Lontir. Boradan has asked you to look from the beacon to Edhellond.\n4\tTalk to Boradan\tBoradan can be found on the beacon, Amon Lontir, just outside Ost Lontir. You have looked upon Edhellond and should now speak to Boradan.\n",
[12497]="70044263\n1\tDefeat Morgul Defilers (total: 5)\tMorgul Defilers can be found in Eryn Lothad. You should defeat defilers to protect the orchard from being ravaged.\n2\tSpeak with Ingold\tIngold can be found at the North-gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Ingold.\n",
[12498]="7005B4A4\n1\tWait with Elta\tElta has suggested to wait and see if Bothin will appear.\n2\tTalk to Elta\tBothin has not appeared. You should talk to Elta and come up with a different plan together.\n3\tFind signs of Bothin\tElta has asked you to find Bothin alone. You should venture into the cave Skrizagáf, on the eastern side of Shataz-kordh.\n4\tYou should continue looking for signs of Bothin in Skrizagáf.\t\n5\tExamine the Orc corpse\tYou have found a dead Orc in Skrizagáf. You should examine the corpse.\n6\tLure out and defeat Bothin\tYou should pretend to steal the Orc corpse and trick Bothin into emerging.\n7\tTalk to Elta near Shataz-kordh\tYou have defeated Bothin and obtained its hide. Elta waits for you outside of Shataz-kordh.\n",
[12499]="7004103F\n1\tTry to free Jajax from his bonds\tJajax is in Abedec's Watch, the Corsair encampment in the ruins south of Dol Amroth. You should free Jajax from his bonds. NOTE: This quest will fail on defeat. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tSpeak with Jajax\tJajax is in the large tent at Abedec's Watch in southern Belfalas. You should speak with Jajax.\n3\tTell Lothíriel of all that transpired\tLothíriel is in the Great Hall of the Prince in Dol Amroth. You should speak with Lothíriel.\n",
[12500]="70062AAD\n1\tMossward has several provisioners, but one of them is usually outside their store-house on the west side of the town square.\t\n2\tTalk to Alla by the north-east side of Mossward\tAlla is by the haystack on the north-east side of Mossward.\n3\tFind Dai in Mossward and talk to him\tDai must be somewhere in Mossward, and with his cheese-filled pockets he is likely to be in real trouble from the town's rodent population.\n4\tTalk to Alla by the north-east side of Mossward\tAlla is by the haystack on the north-east side of Mossward.\n",
[12501]="70001848\n1\tTalk to Orthonn\tOrthonn may be found at the ruins of Ost Lagoros, north-west of Gatson's farm by the river. Farmer Gatson told you that he has been helping the Rangers with provisions for many years and now expects them to help him protect his farm. He has sent you to speak with the Ranger he delivers the food to, a man named Orthonn.\n2\tTalk to Gatson\tGatson awaits you at his farm to the east of Ost Lagoros. Orthonn admitted that Gatson had provisioned them often, but told you that the Rangers did not have the numbers to defend the farms of the North Downs. He asked you to return to Gatson and exhort the farmer and his workhands to flee at once.\n",
[12502]="700604A7\n1\tDefeat threatening foes in the Angle of Mitheithel (total: 6)\tDangerous foes stalk the rocky woodlands of the Angle, and Ravaedron desires for you to help him combat them.\n2\tTalk to Ravaedron along the road from the Trollshaws\tRavaedron is along the road that runs south into the Angle from the Trollshaws.\n3\tFind Fernbrake Cot, the home of Ravaedron's friends, beyond the village of Glynafon to the south-east\tFernbrake Cot, the home of Ravaedron's friends, lies to the south-east, beyond the village of Glynafon in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n4\tTalk to Ravaedron outside Fernbrake Cot\tRavaedron stands outside Fernbrake Cot, the home of his friends, south-east of the old village of Glynafon.\n",
[12503]="70036A35\n1\tAsk Gamling for news\tGamling the Old can be found at Helm's Dike in the southern Westfold. You should ask Gamling for news of the Westfold.\n2\tSpeak with Éomer\tÉomer is at Helm's Dike in the south-eastern Westfold. You should speak with Éomer.\n3\tLearn of the events that changed Théoden's course\tÉomer wishes to relay the counsel of Gandalf, and the news they received upon the road. You should speak with Éomer.\n4\tSpeak with Éomer\tÉomer wishes to speak with you. You should speak with Éomer.\n",
[12504]="7000012F\n1\tFind Hjortur Dourhand\tThe stolen ingot might be found within the walls of Gabilazan. Halmur Stoneshaper suggested you seek the stolen ingot there.\n2\tSearch Hjortur's strongbox for the stolen ingot\tThe stolen ingot might be inside Hjortur's strongbox, within the walls of Gabilazan. You defeated Hjortur Dourhand and should now search the strongbox he guarded for the stolen ingot.\n3\tTalk to Halmur Stoneshaper\030Collect Stolen Dwarf-gold Ingot\tHalmur Stoneshaper is in the tomb of his ancestor on the hill to the left as you approach the dwarf-keep in the pass of Gabilazan from the north. Halmur Stoneshaper is waiting for you to return with the stolen dwarf-gold ingot you retrieved from the descendant of the thief who stole it long ages ago.\n4\tBring the ancient dwarf-chest to Larus Sharpshard\tThe second strongbox is within the tomb of Halmur Stoneshaper in the pass of Gabilazan. Larus Sharpshard is located in a camp north of High Crag. After helping Halmur Stoneshaper reclaim the stolen ingot and fulfil his family's oath, he has allowed you to take the strongbox to bring it to Larus Sharpshard.\n",
[12505]="70046BF6\n1\tHenneth Annûn can be found in north-central North Ithilien. Mablung has asked you to patrol around the borders of Henneth Annûn for possible threats to the refuge.\t\n2\tTalk to Mablung\tMablung can be found in Henneth Annûn. You have scouted the lands surrounding Henneth Annûn and should now report back to Mablung.\n",
[12506]="7000E8BD\n1\tSpeak to Gimli\tHandarod has asked you to gather some allies and seek out the Dwarf Gimli. Gimli will accompany you to the dwarf-keep where the Nazgûl and Skorgrím may be hiding. Gimli is staying in one of the guest rooms along the road that winds up the southern slope of the Vale of Imladris.\n2\tTalk to Glóin\tGlóin is at his camp in the Misty Mountains, north of Rivendell. The Nazgûl left the dwarf-keep, commanding Skorgrím to slay you. Fortunately, you were able to defeat Skorgrím, but a fell spirit emerged from his corpse and cursed the Longbeards before vanishing. You should tell Glóin all that has transpired. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[12507]="70039700\n1\tTalk to Hildulf\tHildulf can be found to the south of the Mead Hall of Middlemead. You have taken up Mágla's burden to rout the agent of Wormtongue in Middlemead. You should speak to Hildulf and the traders of Middlemead.\n",
[12508]="70042B17\n1\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in the Forsaken Inn\030Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in the Forsaken Inn\tTheodore Gorse and Haley Meadowsweet have attracted Bingo's attention in the Forsaken Inn, and he wants to learn more about them.\n2\tTalk to Bingo in the Forsaken Inn\tBingo is in the Forsaken Inn, in the Lone-lands.\n3\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in the Forsaken Inn\tTheodore Gorse is in the Forsaken Inn. Bingo wants to know if Theodore Gorse, self-proclaimed Master Treasure Seeker, will teach him the profession.\n4\tFind the hidden strongbox Theodore could not, somewhere in the Lone-lands\tTheodore gave you a parchment with a riddle on it, apparently a clue to the location of a treasure in the Lone-lands. The parchment reads: 'The torrent flows, blanketed in the shadow of only morning. A sentinel stares from on high; only he still watches. The red squirrel once dared the climb, but Time fells all.'\n5\tBring the cryptic message to Theodore Gorse in the Forsaken Inn\tTheodore Gorse is in the Forsaken Inn. You found the treasure that Theodore Gorse could not, but it was only a parchment of paper with a cryptic message on it. You should bring him the sad news that there was no treasure.\n6\tTalk to Bingo in the Forsaken Inn\tBingo Boffin is in the Forsaken Inn.\n",
[12509]="7001CCD6\n1\tDefeat enemies at the Gostannon (total: 12)\tThe road to the Gostannon lies to the north of Amon Angeled, leading eastwards. Rongal has asked you to utterly destroy the Enemy at the Gostannon.\n2\tTalk to Rongal atop Amon Angened\tRongal is at the Elf-waypost atop Amon Angened, south of the Gostannon. While the Enemy encamped at the Gostannon is greatly weakened, they are still stronger than Rongal surmised. You should return to Rongal with the tidings.\n",
[12510]="7006C575\n1\tComplete the task from Filadal\030Complete the task from Aítarshun\tTharashil asked that you find Aítarshun and Filadal and assist them with the tasks they want to accomplish before they can move forward without pain while they fade from the world.\n2\tReturn to Tharashil and inform them of Filadal and Aítarshun's plight\tYou aided the fading Elves Tharashil asked you to help. You should return to her and tell her of the assistance you provided.\n",
[12511]="70000157\n1\tTalk to Keeper Brombard Foxtail\tBrombard Foxtail is at the Mathom-house in Michel Delving, far west of Tuckborough. Adelard Took asked you to travel to the Mathom-house in Michel Delving and ask Keeper Foxtail for the fireworks rocket he had sent there.\n2\tSet off the fireworks\030Find the Methel-stage in Bywater\tThe Methel-stage is on the southern side of the road heading west out of Bywater. Adelard Took had asked you to fire the rocket off at the Methel-stage in Bywater in hopes that the sight of this last rocket will appease the Old Took's ghost.\n3\tTalk to Adelard Took\tAdelard Took can be found at the Great Smials in Tuckborough. You should return to Adelard Took and let him know that you have done as he asked.\n",
[12512]="700097DD\n1\tBring the Silithar to Aragorn in Rivendell\tAragorn is in one of the guest rooms of the House of Elrond in Rivendell. Calenglad has given you the Silithar to bring to Aragorn. Its light will be used to remake the blade that was broken.\n",
})
